    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Parafibromin-deficient parathryoid tumour",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Morphological features of parafibromin-deficient parathyroid tumours are inconsistent but include a thickened and somewhat hyalinised fibrous capsule, a sheet like growth pattern, eosinophilic cell type and a prominent vasculature. A little microcystic change is noted",
    "source": "Endo&nbsp;5",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/67/95/23863.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/67/95/thumb_23863.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 80529,
    "bookid": 67,
    "chapterId": 95,
    "fileId": 37094,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Parafibromin-deficient parathyroid tumour",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "In contrast to most usual parathyroid adenomas which demonstrate a somewhat nested architecture, parafibromin-deficient parathyroid tumours commonly show a sheet-like architecture with a prominent vasculature.",
    "source": "Endo5",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/67/95/23864.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/67/95/thumb_23864.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 80530,
    "bookid": 67,
    "chapterId": 95,
    "fileId": 37095,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Parafibromin-deficient parathyroid tumour",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Cytological features include nuclear enlargement, perinuclear cytoplasmic clearing and eosinophilic cell type",
    "source": "Endo5",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/67/95/23865.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/67/95/thumb_23865.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 80531,
    "bookid": 67,
    "chapterId": 95,
    "fileId": 37096,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Parafibromin-deficient parathyroid tumour",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Cytological features include nuclear enlargement often with preserved N:C&nbsp;ratios, multinucleation, perinuclear cytoplasmic clearing, and eosinophilic cell type, sometimes with a glassy quality.",
    "source": "Endo5",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/67/95/23866.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/67/95/thumb_23866.jpg"
  },
  {
