    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Parathyroid carcinoma associated with HPTJT syndrome",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "The diagnosis of carcinoma arising in the setting of HPTJT syndrome relies on the same histological criteria as sporadic carcinomas - the demonstration of an unequivocally invasive growth or vascular space invasion. In this instance in addition to invasive growth there neoplastic cells show typical cytological features of a parafbromin-deficient tumour.",
    "source": "Endo5",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/67/95/24104.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/67/95/thumb_24104.jpg"
  },
  {
